  "rationale": "Comparison for unit:given.typing.safety against lean:Unique/TypingSafety:program_safety. program_safety assumes well-formed classes, initial sequence typing and an arbitrary finite execution prefix. It concludes nonstuckness and a counted continuation, with prefixLength plus remaining statements equal to initial code length and a finished final state. This exactly supports the stated total statement-count bound without discarding final owners. Notation and judgment context was checked in unit:given.typing.configurations, unit:given.typing.progress, unit:given.typing.preservation, unit:given.typing.statements.",
